{"turn": 9, "role": "tool", "result": "**[BORROWER ORGANIZATIONAL CHART AND ENTITY DOCUMENTS]{.underline}**\n\n**[Harborview Capital Partners LLC]{.underline}**\n\n**Prepared in Connection with the Construction Loan from Pinnacle Savings Bank, N.A.** **Loan No. CRE-2025-0342**\n\n*Project: \\\"The Piedmont at Brightleaf\\\" --- 601 and 615 Foster Street, Durham, NC 27701*\n\n**January 2025**\n\nPrepared for delivery to Lender\\'s counsel, Ashford, Cromdale Consulting & Laine LLP, in connection with the term sheet executed January 10, 2025.\n\nPrepared by and on behalf of:\n\n> **Calloway & Strauss PLLC** 324 Blackwell Street, Suite 200 Durham, NC 27701\n>\n> Attention: Jonathan F. Ngo, Partner\n>\n> Telephone: (919) 555-4120\n>\n> Email: jngo@callowaystrauss.com\n>\n> *(Borrower\\'s Counsel)*\n\n**[SECTION 1: ORGANIZATIONAL CHART --- HARBORVIEW CAPITAL PARTNERS LLC]{.underline}**\n\n**[1.1 Borrower Entity Overview]{.underline}**\n\n**Harborview Capital Partners LLC** is a limited liability company organized under the laws of the State of North Carolina. The Borrower was formed on **March 14, 2019**, and is registered with the North Carolina Secretary of State under File No. **1923847**. The Borrower\\'s principal office is located at **400 West Main Street, Suite 310, Durham, NC 27701**.\n\nThe Borrower was formed as a single-purpose entity for the acquisition, development, construction, ownership, and operation of the real property located at 601 and 615 Foster Street, Durham, Durham County, North Carolina 27701 (Parcel IDs: 0821-04-72-3341 and 0821-04-72-4102), commonly known as \\\"The Piedmont at Brightleaf\\\" (the \\\"Project\\\"). The current net worth of the Borrower entity is approximately **\\$14,200,000** based on the book value of its assets and liabilities as of the most recent reporting period.\n\nWhile the Borrower was formed as a single-purpose entity and operates exclusively in connection with the Project, the Amended and Restated Operating Agreement of the Borrower (as excerpted in Section 2 below) does not currently include provisions for an independent director or independent manager, nor does it contain separateness covenants customarily associated with single-purpose entity structures in commercial real estate finance transactions. Additionally, as detailed in Section 1.2 below, Brightleaf Investors Group LLC, which holds a 28% membership interest in the Borrower, is an affiliate of Brightleaf Mezzanine Capital LLC, the mezzanine lender to the Project, and both entities are under the common control of Thomas R. Chen. This structural relationship warrants review in the context of SPE separateness analysis.\n\n**[1.2 Member Structure (Ownership Chart)]{.underline}**\n\nThe following sets forth the ownership structure of Harborview Capital Partners LLC as of the date hereof, presented in two tiers reflecting direct membership interests in the Borrower and the control structure of the entity members.\n\n**Tier 1 --- Members of Harborview Capital Partners LLC**\n\n  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  **Member**                       **Type**                           **Membership Interest**   **Role**\n  -------------------------------- ---------------------------------- ------------------------- -----------------\n  Elena Vasquez-Torres             Individual                         62%                       Managing Member\n\n  Brightleaf Investors Group LLC   NC LLC (NC SOS File No. 2045612)   28%                       Member\n\n  Reginald K. Osei                 Individual                         10%                       Member\n  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**Tier 2 --- Control of Brightleaf Investors Group LLC**\n\nBrightleaf Investors Group LLC is a North Carolina limited liability company with its principal office in Durham, North Carolina. The Managing Member of Brightleaf Investors Group LLC is **Thomas R. Chen**. The other members of Brightleaf Investors Group LLC consist of a group of local high-net-worth investors whose identities are available upon request under separate confidentiality agreement.\n\n**Tier 2 --- Affiliate Relationship (Critical Notation)**\n\n**Brightleaf Mezzanine Capital LLC** (NC LLC, NC SOS File No. **2103988**) is an affiliate of Brightleaf Investors Group LLC. Both entities are under the **common control of Thomas R. Chen**, who serves as the Managing Member of both Brightleaf Investors Group LLC and Brightleaf Mezzanine Capital LLC.\n\nBrightleaf Mezzanine Capital LLC is providing a **\\$9,200,000 mezzanine loan** to the Borrower at a fixed rate of **12.50% per annum**, secured by a **pledge of 100% of the membership interests** in the Borrower. The mezzanine loan matures coterminous with the senior construction loan from Pinnacle Savings Bank, N.A. The Borrower\\'s capital structure, accordingly, includes both an equity member (Brightleaf Investors Group LLC, 28%) and a mezzanine lender (Brightleaf Mezzanine Capital LLC), each under the common control of the same individual.\n\n*Note: The mezzanine loan from Brightleaf Mezzanine Capital LLC is secured by a pledge of 100% of the membership interests in the Borrower. An intercreditor agreement between Pinnacle Savings Bank, N.A. and Brightleaf Mezzanine Capital LLC has been negotiated but is not yet executed as of the date hereof.*\n\n**Notation on Guarantors**\n\nThe following individuals have agreed to serve as personal guarantors in connection with the senior construction loan from Pinnacle Savings Bank, N.A.:\n\n**Elena Vasquez-Torres** (62% Member / Managing Member) --- Personal guarantor. Approximate net worth: **\\$29.8 million** (liquid assets: \\$6.1 million; real estate holdings: \\$19.4 million; other assets: \\$4.3 million). Ms. Vasquez-Torres has 22 years of commercial real estate development experience and is a resident of Durham, North Carolina.\n\n**Reginald K. Osei** (10% Member) --- Personal guarantor. Approximate net worth: **\\$11.5 million** (liquid assets: \\$3.2 million; real estate holdings: \\$6.8 million; other assets: \\$1.5 million). Mr. Osei has 15 years of experience in real estate finance and development and is a resident of Chapel Hill, North Carolina.\n\nCombined guarantor net worth: approximately **\\$41.3 million**. Combined guarantor liquidity: **\\$9,300,000** (\\$6.1M + \\$3.2M).\n\n**[1.3 Capital Contributions and Equity Summary]{.underline}**\n\n**Land Contribution.** The real property comprising the Project site (Parcel IDs: 0821-04-72-3341 and 0821-04-72-4102) was contributed to Harborview Capital Partners LLC by **Elena Vasquez-Torres** at a cost basis of **\\$8,200,000**. The land was originally acquired by Ms. Vasquez-Torres in a transaction funded from her personal resources and was subsequently contributed to the Borrower upon formation of the project entity. The contribution was reflected on the Borrower\\'s books at the **\\$8,200,000** acquisition cost basis. For reference, the as-is appraised value of the land per the appraisal by Ridgeline Appraisal Services Inc. dated November 15, 2024 (Appraiser: Linda M. Haverford, MAI) is **\\$8,900,000**, which exceeds the acquisition cost basis by \\$700,000.\n\n**Member Capital Calls.** The members have funded the following capital contributions to date:\n\n  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  **Member**                        **Capital Contribution**                        **Source**\n  --------------------------------- ----------------------------------------------- --------------------------------\n  Elena Vasquez-Torres              \\$8,200,000 (land contribution at cost basis)   Personal acquisition of land\n\n  Brightleaf Investors Group LLC    \\$0 cash to date                                Future capital calls as needed\n\n  Reginald K. Osei                  \\$0 cash to date                                Future capital calls as needed\n\n  **Total member equity to date**   **\\$8,200,000**                                 \n  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**Additional Funding Sources.** The total project cost for The Piedmont at Brightleaf is **\\$56,700,000**. Beyond the member equity reflected above, the Project is funded as follows:\n\n> • Senior construction loan (Pinnacle Savings Bank, N.A.): **\\$47,500,000**\n>\n> • Mezzanine loan (Brightleaf Mezzanine Capital LLC): **\\$9,200,000**\n>\n> • Additional borrower cash equity: **\\$0**\n>\n> • **Total: \\$47,500,000 + \\$9,200,000 + \\$0 = \\$56,700,000**\n\nThe foregoing sources and uses summary reflects that there is no additional cash equity contribution from any member beyond the land contribution by Ms. Vasquez-Torres. The entire non-debt funding of the Project consists of the \\$8,200,000 land contribution. Brightleaf Investors Group LLC, the 28% member affiliated with the mezzanine lender, has contributed no cash equity to date; its membership interest was issued in consideration of its commitment to arrange third-party mezzanine financing for the Project, as set forth in the Operating Agreement (see Section 2.3 below). The mezzanine loan of \\$9,200,000 from Brightleaf Mezzanine Capital LLC, an affiliate of Brightleaf Investors Group LLC, fills the gap between the senior loan proceeds and the total project cost. No independent cash equity beyond the land contribution exists in the capital stack.\n\n**[SECTION 2: EXCERPTS FROM OPERATING AGREEMENT OF HARBORVIEW CAPITAL PARTNERS LLC]{.underline}**\n\n**[2.1 Preamble and Identification]{.underline}**\n\nThe following are selected excerpts from the Amended and Restated Operating Agreement of Harborview Capital Partners LLC, dated as of March 14, 2019, as amended through December 1, 2024 (the \\\"Operating Agreement\\\"). These excerpts are provided for informational purposes only in connection with the senior construction loan from Pinnacle Savings Bank, N.A. (Loan No. CRE-2025-0342) and do not constitute the complete Operating Agreement. The full Operating Agreement has been provided to Lender\\'s counsel, Ashford, Cromdale Consulting & Laine LLP, under separate cover. In the event of any conflict between these excerpts and the full Operating Agreement, the full Operating Agreement shall control.\n\n**[2.2 Excerpt --- Article III: Management and Authority (Section 3.1 --- Managing Member)]{.underline}**\n\nThe following is excerpted from Article III, Section 3.1 of the Operating Agreement:\n\n> *Section 3.1 --- Managing Member.* **Elena Vasquez-Torres** shall serve as the sole Managing Member of the Company. The Managing Member shall have the exclusive authority to manage the day-to-day operations and affairs of the Company, including without limitation: (a) entering into contracts on behalf of the Company in the ordinary course of business; (b) hiring and terminating employees, contractors, and consultants; (c) making capital expenditure decisions with respect to the Project in amounts not exceeding Five Hundred Thousand Dollars (\\$500,000) individually (any single expenditure in excess of \\$500,000 shall require the prior approval of Members holding a majority in interest of the outstanding membership interests); (d) executing loan documents, promissory notes, deeds of trust, and related instruments on behalf of the Company; and (e) managing and overseeing the construction and development of the Project, including selection of architects, general contractors, and subcontractors.\n>\n> *Section 3.2 --- Major Decisions.* Notwithstanding the foregoing, the following actions shall require the prior written approval of Members holding at least seventy-five percent (75%) of the outstanding membership interests: (a) any sale, transfer, or encumbrance of all or substantially all of the Company\\'s assets; (b) any financing or refinancing of the Property in a principal amount in excess of One Million Dollars (\\$1,000,000); (c) the admission of any new Member to the Company; (d) any amendment to this Operating Agreement; and (e) any voluntary dissolution of the Company or the filing of any petition for relief under any federal or state bankruptcy or insolvency law.\n\nThe approval threshold of 75% means that Elena Vasquez-Torres (62%) cannot unilaterally approve any major decision. She would require the concurrence of at least one additional member. Combined with Brightleaf Investors Group LLC (28%), the two members hold 90%, which exceeds the 75% threshold. Combined with Reginald K. Osei (10%), Ms. Vasquez-Torres and Mr. Osei hold 72%, which falls below the 75% threshold. Consequently, Brightleaf Investors Group LLC holds an effective veto right over major decisions, as no combination of the other two members alone can reach the required supermajority.\n\nThe Operating Agreement, as currently in effect, does not contain any provision requiring the appointment of an independent director or independent manager for the Company. There are no separateness covenants requiring the Company to maintain its own books, records, and bank accounts separate from those of its members or their affiliates, no prohibition on commingling of funds with affiliates, and no requirement that the Company obtain a non-consolidation opinion. These provisions are customarily required by institutional lenders in single-purpose entity structures.\n\n**[2.3 Excerpt --- Article V: Capital Contributions (Section 5.1 --- Initial Capital Contributions; Section 5.3 --- Additional Capital Calls)]{.underline}**\n\nThe following is excerpted from Article V, Sections 5.1 and 5.3 of the Operating Agreement:\n\n> *Section 5.1 --- Initial Capital Contributions.* Each Member shall make the following initial capital contributions to the Company:\n>\n> \\(a\\) **Elena Vasquez-Torres** shall contribute that certain real property located at 601 and 615 Foster Street, Durham, Durham County, North Carolina 27701 (Parcel IDs: 0821-04-72-3341 and 0821-04-72-4102), together with all improvements, easements, and appurtenances thereto, valued at Eight Million Two Hundred Thousand Dollars (\\$8,200,000) (acquisition cost basis), in exchange for a sixty-two percent (62%) membership interest in the Company.\n>\n> \\(b\\) **Brightleaf Investors Group LLC** shall make an initial capital contribution of Zero Dollars (\\$0) at the time of formation. Brightleaf Investors Group LLC shall receive a twenty-eight percent (28%) membership interest in the Company in consideration of its commitment to arrange third-party mezzanine financing for the Project and to contribute future capital as and when called by the Managing Member in accordance with Section 5.3 of this Agreement.\n>\n> \\(c\\) **Reginald K. Osei** shall make an initial capital contribution of Zero Dollars (\\$0) at the time of formation. Reginald K. Osei shall receive a ten percent (10%) membership interest in the Company in consideration of development management services to be provided to the Company in connection with the Project and his commitment to contribute future capital as and when called by the Managing Member in accordance with Section 5.3 of this Agreement.\n>\n> *Section 5.3 --- Additional Capital Calls.* The Managing Member may, from time to time, issue capital calls to all Members pro rata in proportion to their respective membership interests, upon not less than thirty (30) days\\' prior written notice. Capital calls shall be at the sole discretion of the Managing Member for purposes of funding Project costs not covered by loan proceeds or other available funds. Any Member who fails to fund a capital call within the applicable notice period shall be subject to dilution of such Member\\'s membership interest on a two-to-one (2:1) penalty basis, as calculated in accordance with Schedule B attached hereto.\n\nAs reflected above, Brightleaf Investors Group LLC received its 28% membership interest not in exchange for a cash capital contribution but in consideration of its commitment to arrange third-party mezzanine financing for the Project. That mezzanine financing was arranged through Brightleaf Mezzanine Capital LLC, an entity under the common control of Thomas R. Chen, who also serves as Managing Member of Brightleaf Investors Group LLC. The Borrower\\'s cash equity position is therefore entirely dependent on the land contribution made by Elena Vasquez-Torres.\n\n**[2.4 Excerpt --- Article VI: Distributions (Section 6.1 --- Distribution Waterfall)]{.underline}**\n\nThe following is excerpted from Article VI, Section 6.1 of the Operating Agreement:\n\n> *Section 6.1 --- Distribution Waterfall.* Distributable Cash (as defined in Section 1.1 of this Agreement, being the net cash from operations of the Company or net proceeds from a Capital Event, in each case after payment of all Company obligations, including without limitation debt service on all loans (including the senior construction loan, any mezzanine or subordinate financing, and any other indebtedness of the Company), required reserves, and operating expenses) shall be distributed to the Members in the following order of priority:\n>\n> \\(a\\) **First**, to all Members pro rata in proportion to their respective membership interests, until each Member has received a cumulative return equal to a nine percent (9.0%) per annum preferred return on such Member\\'s unreturned capital contribution (as calculated on a non-compounded basis from the date of such contribution);\n>\n> \\(b\\) **Second**, to all Members pro rata in proportion to their respective membership interests, until each Member has received a return of one hundred percent (100%) of such Member\\'s unreturned capital contribution; and\n>\n> \\(c\\) **Third**, the balance, if any, shall be distributed seventy percent (70%) to Elena Vasquez-Torres (as the Managing Member), twenty percent (20%) to Brightleaf Investors Group LLC, and ten percent (10%) to Reginald K. Osei (the \\\"Promote Split\\\").\n\nThe distribution waterfall expressly provides that debt service on \\\"all loans,\\\" including any mezzanine or subordinate financing, constitutes a Company obligation that must be satisfied before any distributions are made to the Members. This structure places the mezzanine loan from Brightleaf Mezzanine Capital LLC --- an affiliate of the 28% member, Brightleaf Investors Group LLC --- at a priority ahead of member distributions, further intertwining the financial relationship between the Borrower, its equity members, and the mezzanine lender.\n\n**[2.5 Excerpt --- Article IX: Transfer Restrictions (Section 9.1 --- Restrictions on Transfer)]{.underline}**\n\nThe following is excerpted from Article IX, Section 9.1 of the Operating Agreement:\n\n> *Section 9.1 --- Restrictions on Transfer.* No Member may sell, assign, transfer, pledge, encumber, hypothecate, or otherwise dispose of all or any portion of such Member\\'s membership interest in the Company without the prior written consent of the Managing Member and Members holding at least seventy-five percent (75%) of the outstanding membership interests. Notwithstanding the foregoing, a Member may pledge such Member\\'s membership interest to a lender as collateral for a bona fide loan, provided that such pledge has been approved in writing by the Managing Member. Any purported transfer in violation of this Section 9.1 shall be null and void and of no force or effect.\n\nThe Operating Agreement permits pledges of membership interests with Managing Member approval but does not distinguish between a pledge to the senior lender and a pledge to the mezzanine lender, nor does it address relative priority between competing pledges of the same membership interests. As noted in Section 1.2 above, the mezzanine lender (Brightleaf Mezzanine Capital LLC) currently holds a pledge of 100% of the membership interests in the Borrower as security for the mezzanine loan. If the senior construction lender, Pinnacle Savings Bank, N.A., also requires a pledge of 100% of the membership interests as collateral for the senior loan, the Operating Agreement provides no mechanism to resolve conflicting first-priority claims on the same collateral. The resolution of priority as between the competing pledges is expected to be addressed by the intercreditor agreement between Pinnacle Savings Bank, N.A. and Brightleaf Mezzanine Capital LLC, which has been negotiated but is not yet executed as of the date hereof.\n\n**[SECTION 3: CERTIFICATION AND CONTACT INFORMATION]{.underline}**\n\nThe undersigned, as Managing Member of Harborview Capital Partners LLC, hereby certifies that the foregoing organizational chart is true, correct, and complete in all material respects as of the date hereof, and that the excerpts from the Operating Agreement set forth above are true, correct, and complete excerpts from the Amended and Restated Operating Agreement of Harborview Capital Partners LLC, dated as of March 14, 2019, as amended through December 1, 2024, as currently in effect. The undersigned further certifies that there have been no amendments to the Operating Agreement since December 1, 2024, and that no events have occurred since such date that would materially alter the organizational structure, membership interests, or governance provisions described herein.\n\nHARBORVIEW CAPITAL PARTNERS LLC\n\nBy: **\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_**\n\nName: Elena Vasquez-Torres\n\nTitle: Managing Member\n\nDate: **\\_\\_\\_**\\_, 2025\n\n**Contact Information for Borrower\\'s Counsel:**\n\n> Jonathan F. Ngo, Partner Calloway & Strauss PLLC 324 Blackwell Street, Suite 200 Durham, NC 27701 Telephone: (919) 555-4120 Facsimile: (919) 555-4121\n>\n> Email: jngo@callowaystrauss.com\n", "tool_call_id": "call_00_fJUX77y2mnGDg2LwXI985813", "tool_name": "read", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"documents/borrower-org-chart.docx\"}"}
