{"turn": 13, "role": "assistant", "text": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_i2f1kZnDO9TP3bNBueTA7759", "name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && cat > p1.md <<'MD'\\n::: {custom-style=\\\"Title\\\"}\\nCONSTRUCTION-TO-MINI-PERMANENT LOAN AGREEMENT\\n:::\\n\\n::: {custom-style=\\\"Subtitle\\\"}\\nTHE PIEDMONT AT BRIGHTLEAF — 601 AND 615 FOSTER STREET, DURHAM, NORTH CAROLINA\\n:::\\n\\n::: {custom-style=\\\"Subtitle\\\"}\\nby and between HARBORVIEW CAPITAL PARTNERS LLC, as Borrower, and PINNACLE SAVINGS BANK, N.A., as Lender\\n:::\\n\\n|  |  |\\n|:---|:---|\\n| **Lender:** | Pinnacle Savings Bank, N.A., a national banking association |\\n| **Lender's Loan No.:** | CRE-2025-0342 |\\n| **Borrower:** | Harborview Capital Partners LLC, a North Carolina limited liability company |\\n| **Loan Amount:** | $[47,500,000] (see Section 2.6 as to reduction of the Commitment) |\\n| **Guarantors:** | Elena Vasquez-Torres and Reginald K. Osei |\\n| **Property:** | 601 and 615 Foster Street, Durham, Durham County, North Carolina 27701 (Durham County Parcel IDs 0821-04-72-3341 and 0821-04-72-4102) |\\n| **Target Closing Date:** | February 28, 2025 |\\n| **Draft Date:** | Prepared by Ashford, Cromdale Consulting & Laine LLP, counsel to the Lender |\\n| **Status:** | **WORKING DRAFT — FOR DISCUSSION ONLY — NOT AN OFFER; SUBJECT TO CREDIT APPROVAL, DILIGENCE AND DOCUMENTATION** |\\n\\n::: {custom-style=\\\"DraftNote\\\"}\\n**PRELIMINARY NOTE TO THIS DRAFT.** This draft has been prepared from, and is intended to give effect to, (i) the Term Sheet dated January 10, 2025 executed by the Lender and the Borrower, (ii) the Senior Loan Committee Credit Memorandum dated January 22, 2025 for Loan No. CRE-2025-0342 (the \\\"Credit Memorandum\\\"), (iii) the appraisal of Ridgeline Appraisal Services Inc. dated November 15, 2024 (File RAS-2024-1147), (iv) the Preliminary Title Commitment of Aldersgate Title & Escrow Inc. No. NC-2024-88712 effective December 5, 2024, (v) the Phase I Environmental Site Assessment of Sentinel Environmental Consulting LLC dated October 28, 2024 (Project SEC-2024-1147) and the Phase II investigation it summarises, (vi) the Borrower's organizational chart and operating agreement excerpts dated January 2025, and (vii) the Borrower's construction budget and draw schedule dated January 8, 2025. The source documents do not agree in all respects. Where the record is internally inconsistent or silent, this draft adopts a position, states it in brackets, and flags the point in a \\\"Drafting Note\\\" cross-referenced to the issue numbering used in our accompanying cover memorandum of even date. **All bracketed amounts, dates and alternative formulations remain subject to business-term agreement and to the Lender's credit approval; no bracketed item is to be treated as finally negotiated.** Nothing in the source documents constitutes a binding commitment by the Lender except Sections 22 and 23 of the Term Sheet.\\n:::\\n\\n::: {custom-style=\\\"Title\\\"}\\nTABLE OF ARTICLES\\n:::\\n\\n| Article | Heading |\\n|:--|:--|\\n| 1 | Definitions and Interpretation |\\n| 2 | The Loan; Commitment; Purpose |\\n| 3 | Interest, Fees, Yield Protection and Payments |\\n| 4 | Conditions Precedent to Closing |\\n| 5 | Conditions Precedent to Each Advance; Draw Mechanics |\\n| 6 | Disbursement; Approved Budget; Change Orders; Retainage |\\n| 7 | Interest Reserve Account; Equity Deposit Account |\\n| 8 | Representations and Warranties |\\n| 9 | Affirmative Covenants |\\n| 10 | Negative Covenants |\\n| 11 | Financial Covenants and Reporting |\\n| 12 | Single-Purpose Entity and Separateness Covenants |\\n| 13 | Environmental Matters; NFA Letter Compliance |\\n| 14 | Collateral; Security Documents; Pledged Interests; Intercreditor Matters |\\n| 15 | Guaranties |\\n| 16 | Events of Default |\\n| 17 | Remedies |\\n| 18 | Indemnification; Expenses; Environmental Indemnity |\\n| 19 | Insurance and Condemnation |\\n| 20 | Leasing and Operation of the Property |\\n| 21 | Extension Option |\\n| 22 | Notices; Governing Law; Miscellaneous |\\n\\n# ARTICLE 1 — DEFINITIONS AND INTERPRETATION\\n\\n## 1.1 Defined Terms.\\n\\nAs used in this Agreement, the following terms have the following meanings:\\n\\n::: {custom-style=\\\"SubPara\\\"}\\n(a) \\\"**Advance**\\\" means each disbursement of the Loan proceeds made or to be made by the Lender under this Agreement, including the Initial Advance and each subsequent Draw, and \\\"**Advances**\\\" means all of them collectively.\\n\\n(b) \\\"**Affiliate**\\\" means, with respect to any Person, any other Person that directly or indirectly controls, is controlled by, or is under common control with such Person, and, if such Person is an individual, any member of such individual's immediate family. \\\"**Control**\\\" means the possession, directly or indirectly, of the power to direct or cause the direction of the management or policies of a Person, whether through ownership of voting securities, by contract or otherwise.\\n\\n(c) \\\"**Agreement**\\\" means this Construction-to-Mini-Permanent Loan Agreement, as amended, restated, supplemented or otherwise modified from time to time.\\n\\n(d) \\\"**Approved Budget**\\\" means the project budget for the Project attached as **Schedule 3**, as the same may be revised from time to time only with the Lender's prior written consent in accordance with Section 6.3, showing, by line item, all Project Costs and the sources of funding therefor.\\n\\n(e) \\\"**Approved Plans**\\\" means the plans and specifications for the Project prepared by the Architect and identified on **Schedule 3-A**, as approved by the Lender and as the same may be modified only in accordance with Section 6.4.\\n\\n(f) \\\"**Architect**\\\" means Meridian Design Collective PC, a North Carolina professional corporation, and its permitted successors and assigns.\\n\\n(g) \\\"**As-Completed Value**\\\" means the \\\"as-completed\\\" market value of the Project as concluded in the Appraisal, being **$72,800,000**, determined on a prospective basis as of August 31, 2027.\\n\\n(h) \\\"**As-Stabilized Value**\\\" means the \\\"as-stabilized\\\" market value of the Project as concluded in the Appraisal (assuming ninety-five percent (95%) occupancy), being **$76,200,000**.\\n\\n(i) \\\"**Appraisal**\\\" means the self-contained appraisal report of the Property dated November 15, 2024 prepared by Ridgeline Appraisal Services Inc. (Linda M. Haverford, MAI; File RAS-2024-1147), together with any update, addendum, recertification or replacement appraisal obtained in accordance with this Agreement.\\n\\n(j) \\\"**Business Day**\\\" means any day other than a Saturday, a Sunday or a day on which commercial banks are authorized or required to be closed in Charlotte, North Carolina or New York, New York; and, for purposes of determining SOFR, any day that is also a U.S. Government Securities Business Day.\\n\\n(k) \\\"**Capital Event**\\\" means any sale, refinancing, recapitalization, contribution, syndication or other capital transaction involving the Borrower, the Property or any direct or indirect interest therein, other than the Loan and the Mezzanine Loan.\\n\\n(l) \\\"**Closing**\\\" and \\\"**Closing Date**\\\" mean the date on which the initial funding of the Loan occurs, which the parties anticipate will be **February 28, 2025**.\\n\\n(m) \\\"**Code**\\\" means the Internal Revenue Code of 1986, as amended.\\n\\n(n) \\\"**Commitment**\\\" means the Lender's commitment to make Advances in an aggregate principal amount not to exceed the Loan Amount, as the same may be reduced in accordance with Section 2.6 or Section 3.6.\\n\\n(o) \\\"**Completion Date**\\\" means the date on which Substantial Completion has occurred and all conditions to the Final Advance set out in Section 5.9 have been satisfied.\\n\\n(p) \\\"**Construction Contract**\\\" means the guaranteed maximum price construction contract dated [_________], 20[__] between the Borrower and the Contractor, in the guaranteed maximum price amount of **$34,750,000**, together with all amendments, change orders and supplements thereto approved in accordance with Section 6.4.\\n\\n(q) \\\"**Construction Maturity Date**\\\" means [**August 28, 2027**] [*Alternative, if the parties accept the schedule correction described in Drafting Note 2: **December 31, 2027***], being the last day of the Construction Period.\\n\\n(r) \\\"**Construction Period**\\\" means the period commencing on the Closing Date and ending on the Construction Maturity Date.\\n\\n(s) \\\"**Construction Schedule**\\\" means the construction schedule and milestone table attached as **Schedule 10**, as updated from time to time with the Lender's consent in accordance with Section 9.1(l).\\n\\n(t) \\\"**Contingency**\\\" means the line items for hard cost contingency and soft cost contingency set out in the Approved Budget, in the aggregate amount of **$1,440,000** (comprising a hard cost contingency of $1,140,000 and a soft cost contingency of $300,000), which may be disbursed only in accordance with Section 6.5.\\n\\n(u) \\\"**Contractor**\\\" means Graystone Construction Group Inc., a North Carolina corporation (NC General Contractor License No. 78442), and its permitted successors and assigns.\\n\\n(v) \\\"**Default Rate**\\\" means, on any day, a rate per annum equal to the sum of (i) the rate of interest otherwise applicable to the Loan on such day under Section 3.1 or Section 3.2, as applicable, plus (ii) five percent (5.00%).\\n\\n(w) \\\"**Developer Fee**\\\" means the developer fee payable to the Borrower in the aggregate amount of **$2,835,000** as set forth in the Approved Budget, of which not more than **$1,835,000** may be funded from Loan proceeds and $1,000,000 of which is to be funded from sources other than Loan proceeds.\\n\\n(x) \\\"**Draw**\\\" means an Advance (other than the Initial Advance) made during the Construction Period in respect of hard or soft Project Costs, in accordance with Article 5 and the Draw Schedule.\\n\\n(y) \\\"**Draw Request**\\\" means a written request for an Advance substantially in the form of **Exhibit A**, accompanied by the certificates and documents required by Section 5.4.\\n\\n(z) \\\"**Draw Schedule**\\\" means the schedule of Advances attached as **Schedule 4**, as the same may be adjusted in accordance with Section 6.2.\\n\\n::: {custom-style=\\\"SubPara\\\"}\\n(aa) \\\"**Environmental Indemnity**\\\" means the Environmental Indemnity Agreement of even date herewith executed by the Borrower and each Guarantor in favour of the Lender.\\n\\n(bb) \\\"**Environmental Laws**\\\" means all federal, state and local laws, statutes, regulations, rules, ordinances, orders, directives, permits, licences and judgments relating to pollution, the protection of human health or the environment, or the use, generation, storage, treatment, transportation, disposal or release of Hazardous Materials, including CERCLA (42 U.S.C. §9601 et seq.), the Resource Conservation and Recovery Act (42 U.S.C. §6901 et seq.), the North Carolina Inactive Hazardous Sites Response Act (N.C.G.S. §130A-310 et seq.), the North Carolina Oil Pollution and Hazardous Substances Control Act (N.C.G.S. §143-215.75 et seq.) and the North Carolina Sedimentation Pollution Control Act (N.C.G.S. §113A-50 et seq.).\\n\\n(cc) \\\"**Equity Deposit**\\\" means the funds required to be deposited by the Borrower in the Equity Deposit Account pursuant to Section 7.6, in the amount of **$[2,140,000]** [*see Drafting Note 1(d) and Section 2.6 as to the amount, the source and the application of such funds*].\\n\\n(dd) \\\"**Equity Deposit Account**\\\" means the deposit account maintained by the Lender as described in Section 7.6.\\n\\n(ee) \\\"**Event of Default**\\\" means any event described in Article 16.\\n\\n(ff) \\\"**Existing Mortgage**\\\" means the deed of trust dated September 14, 2018 recorded in Book 6215, Page 892, Durham County Registry, from Foster Street Properties LLC to the trustee named therein for the benefit of Triangle Commercial Bank, securing an original principal indebtedness of **$3,400,000**, together with all modifications, extensions and renewals thereof.\\n\\n(gg) \\\"**Existing Mortgage Payoff Amount**\\\" means the aggregate amount required to satisfy and discharge the Existing Mortgage in full at Closing, as evidenced by a payoff letter from the holder thereof dated not more than thirty (30) days before the Closing Date and acceptable to the Title Company, comprising principal, accrued interest, per diem, prepayment or exit charges and the holder's reasonable costs.\\n\\n(hh) \\\"**Final Advance**\\\" means the release of Retainage described in Section 5.9 and Section 6.7.\\n\\n(ii) \\\"**Fiscal Year**\\\" means the calendar year or such other twelve-month period as the Borrower may adopt with the Lender's prior written consent.\\n\\n(jj) \\\"**GAAP**\\\" means generally accepted accounting principles in the United States, consistently applied.\\n\\n(kk) \\\"**Governmental Authority**\\\" means any federal, state, county, municipal or other governmental or quasi-governmental authority, agency, department, board, commission or instrumentality having jurisdiction over the Borrower, any Guarantor, the Property or the Project, including the City of Durham, Durham County, the State of North Carolina, the NCDEQ and the OCC.\\n\\n(ll) \\\"**Guarantor**\\\" means each of Elena Vasquez-Torres and Reginald K. Osei, and \\\"**Guarantors**\\\" means both of them, jointly and severally, together with any additional or substitute guarantor approved by the Lender.\\n\\n(mm) \\\"**Guaranty**\\\" means, individually and collectively, the Completion Guaranty, the Carry Guaranty, the Partial Repayment Guaranty, the Environmental Indemnity and each other guaranty, indemnity or surety agreement now or hereafter delivered by any Guarantor in favour of the Lender.\\n\\n(nn) \\\"**Hazardous Materials**\\\" means any substance, material or waste regulated under any Environmental Law, including petroleum and petroleum products, petroleum-derived compounds (including total petroleum hydrocarbons, benzene, toluene, ethylbenzene and xylenes), asbestos, polychlorinated biphenyls, per- and polyfluoroalkyl substances, radon and mould.\\n\\n(oo) \\\"**Indebtedness**\\\" means, for any Person, all obligations for borrowed money, all obligations evidenced by notes, bonds or similar instruments, all capitalised lease obligations, all guarantees of the obligations of others, all reimbursement obligations in respect of letters of credit, and all other obligations that would be classified as indebtedness under GAAP.\\n\\n(pp) \\\"**Inspection Consultant**\\\" means the independent third-party construction inspection firm engaged by the Lender at the Borrower's expense pursuant to Section 9.1(m), and any successor engaged by the Lender.\\n\\n(qq) \\\"**Interest Reserve**\\\" means the interest reserve in the original amount of **$[4,850,000]** established and maintained in accordance with Article 7 [*see Drafting Note 3 as to the adequacy of such amount*].\\n\\n(rr) \\\"**Interest Reserve Account**\\\" means the segregated sub-account of the Lender's books maintained in respect of the Loan and designated as the Interest Reserve Account pursuant to Section 7.1.\\n\\n(ss) \\\"**Land**\\\" means the real property described on **Schedule 1**, comprising Durham County Parcel IDs 0821-04-72-3341 (601 Foster Street) and 0821-04-72-4102 (615 Foster Street), as more particularly described by the Survey to be delivered pursuant to Section 4.1(i).\\n\\n(tt) \\\"**Leases**\\\" means all present and future leases, licences, concessions and occupancy agreements of any part of the Property, together with all guaranties, letters of credit, security deposits and other security therefor.\\n\\n(uu) \\\"**Lender**\\\" means Pinnacle Savings Bank, N.A., a national banking association, and its successors and assigns, including any assignee or participant of any interest in the Loan.\\n\\n(vv) \\\"**Lien**\\\" means any mortgage, deed of trust, deed to secure debt, pledge, security interest, hypothecation, assignment, encumbrance, lien (statutory or otherwise, including any claim of lien under N.C.G.S. Chapter 44A), charge, easement, restriction, covenant, condition or other preferential arrangement of any kind or nature.\\n\\n(ww) \\\"**Loan**\\\" means the construction-to-mini-permanent loan made by the Lender to the Borrower under this Agreement in the aggregate principal amount of the Loan Amount, together with all accrued interest, fees, costs, expenses and other amounts owing hereunder or under the other Loan Documents.\\n\\n(xx) \\\"**Loan Amount**\\\" means **$[47,500,000]**, as the same may be permanently reduced pursuant to Section 2.6 or Section 3.6.\\n\\n(yy) \\\"**Loan Documents**\\\" means this Agreement, the Note, the Deed of Trust, the Assignment of Rents, the Security Agreement, the UCC-1 financing statements, the Pledge Agreement, the Assignment of Construction Contract, the Assignment of Architect's Contract, the Collateral Assignment of Insurance and Condemnation Proceeds, each Guaranty, the Environmental Indemnity, the Intercreditor Agreement, each Subordination, Non-Disturbance and Attornment Agreement, each Compliance Certificate, each Title Policy, and each other document, instrument, certificate or agreement now or hereafter executed or delivered in connection with the Loan, as each may be amended, restated or supplemented.\\n\\n(zz) \\\"**Material Adverse Effect**\\\" means any event, circumstance, change or condition that, individually or in the aggregate, (i) has or could reasonably be expected to have a material adverse effect on the business, assets, liabilities, financial condition, operations or prospects of the Borrower, any Guarantor or the Project, (ii) materially impairs the value, use, occupancy or operation of the Property, (iii) materially impairs the ability of the Borrower or any Guarantor to perform its obligations under the Loan Documents, or (iv) materially impairs the enforceability, validity, perfection or priority of the Lender's Liens on the Collateral.\\n\\n::: {custom-style=\\\"SubPara\\\"}\\n(aaa) \\\"**Maturity Date**\\\" means the Mini-Perm Maturity Date, as the same may be extended pursuant to Article 21.\\n\\n(bbb) \\\"**Mezzanine Lender**\\\" means Brightleaf Mezzanine Capital LLC, a North Carolina limited liability company (NC Secretary of State File No. 2103988), and its successors and assigns.\\n\\n(ccc) \\\"**Mezzanine Loan**\\\" means the mezzanine loan in the principal amount of **$9,200,000** made or to be made by the Mezzanine Lender to the Borrower, bearing interest at the fixed rate of **12.50%** per annum and evidenced and secured by the Mezzanine Loan Documents.\\n\\n(ddd) \\\"**Mezzanine Loan Documents**\\\" means the mezzanine loan agreement, promissory note, pledge agreement and all other documents evidencing, securing or relating to the Mezzanine Loan.\\n\\n(eee) \\\"**Mini-Perm Maturity Date**\\\" means **August 28, 2028**, as the same may be extended to **February 28, 2029** in accordance with Article 21.\\n\\n(fff) \\\"**Mini-Perm Period**\\\" means the period commencing on the day following the Construction Maturity Date (or, if earlier, the date on which Substantial Completion has occurred and the Loan has converted to the Mini-Perm Period in accordance with Section 2.5) and ending on the Maturity Date.\\n\\n(ggg) \\\"**NCDEQ**\\\" means the North Carolina Department of Environmental Quality, Inactive Hazardous Sites Branch, and any successor agency.\\n\\n(hhh) \\\"**NFA Letter**\\\" means the No Further Action determination letter issued by NCDEQ dated **September 30, 2024** in respect of Site ID IHSB-24-1203 / Incident No. NONUST-24-0847, together with all conditions, restrictions and requirements thereof, as the same may be modified by NCDEQ in writing.\\n\\n(iii) \\\"**Note**\\\" means the promissory note of even date herewith in the original principal amount of the Loan Amount, executed by the Borrower in favour of the Lender.\\n\\n(jjj) \\\"**OCC**\\\" means the Office of the Comptroller of the Currency.\\n\\n(kkk) \\\"**Permitted Exceptions**\\\" means the matters listed on **Schedule 2**, being the exceptions to title approved by the Lender and insured against (or excepted) under the Title Policy, and no others.\\n\\n(lll) \\\"**Person**\\\" means any individual, corporation, partnership, joint venture, limited liability company, association, trust, unincorporated organisation, Governmental Authority or other entity.\\n\\n(mmm) \\\"**Phase I ESA**\\\" means the Phase I Environmental Site Assessment of the Property dated October 28, 2024 prepared by Sentinel Environmental Consulting LLC (Project SEC-2024-1147) in accordance with ASTM E1527-21 and 40 C.F.R. Part 312, together with the reliance letter in favour of the Lender referenced therein.\\n\\n(nnn) \\\"**Phase II ESA**\\\" means the Phase II Environmental Site Assessment of the Property dated August 30, 2024 prepared by Sentinel Environmental Consulting LLC (Project SEC-2024-1089), including the soil, groundwater and soil gas sampling results summarised in the Phase I ESA.\\n\\n(ooo) \\\"**Pledge Agreement**\\\" means the pledge and security agreement of even date herewith pursuant to which each member of the Borrower pledges to the Lender one hundred percent (100%) of the Pledged Interests.\\n\\n(ppp) \\\"**Pledged Interests**\\\" means one hundred percent (100%) of the membership interests in the Borrower, whether now owned or hereafter acquired, held by Elena Vasquez-Torres (62%), Brightleaf Investors Group LLC (28%) and Reginald K. Osei (10%), together with all distributions, proceeds and substitutions thereof.\\n\\n(qqq) \\\"**Project**\\\" means the acquisition, development, construction and operation on the Land of a six-storey Class A mixed-use development comprising 212 residential units (142 one-bedroom, 56 two-bedroom and 14 three-bedroom), approximately 18,400 square feet of ground-floor retail space in seven bays, a four-level structured parking garage containing 276 spaces, and related amenities, comprising approximately 287,500 square feet of gross building area, together with all site work, infrastructure, improvements, fixtures and personal property related thereto.\\n\\n(rrr) \\\"**Project Costs**\\\" means all costs and expenses incurred or to be incurred in connection with the acquisition, development, construction, equipping, completion, leasing and operation of the Project, including all amounts shown in the Approved Budget.\\n\\n(sss) \\\"**Retainage**\\\" means an amount equal to ten percent (10%) of each Advance in respect of hard construction costs, withheld by the Lender in accordance with Section 6.6, which amount shall in the aggregate equal **$3,475,000** (being ten percent (10%) of the guaranteed maximum price under the Construction Contract) if the Construction Contract is performed in full at the guaranteed maximum price, subject to adjustment for approved change orders.\\n\\n(ttt) \\\"**SOFR**\\\" means the Secured Overnight Financing Rate published by the Federal Reserve Bank of New York (or a successor administrator selected by the Lender in its reasonable discretion) for the applicable U.S. Government Securities Business Day, provided that in no event shall SOFR be less than the **SOFR Floor of 1.00%** per annum.\\n\\n(uuu) \\\"**Substantial Completion**\\\" means the substantial completion of the Project in accordance with the Approved Plans, evidenced by (i) the Architect's certificate of substantial completion (AIA G704 or equivalent), (ii) the issuance of a temporary or final certificate of occupancy by the City of Durham for all residential units and retail bays, and (iii) the Inspection Consultant's written confirmation that the Project is substantially complete and that all remaining work and punch-list items are covered by retained funds.\\n\\n(vvv) \\\"**Survey**\\\" means an ALTA/NSPS Land Title Survey of the Land prepared in accordance with the 2021 ALTA/NSPS Minimum Standard Detail Requirements (including such Table A optional items as the Lender may require), certified to the Lender, the Borrower and the Title Company, dated or re-certified within ninety (90) days before the Closing Date, prepared by a surveyor licensed in North Carolina.\\n\\n(www) \\\"**Title Company**\\\" means Aldersgate Title & Escrow Inc. (Escrow Officer: Patricia Langley), or such other title insurance company acceptable to the Lender.\\n\\n(xxx) \\\"**Title Policy**\\\" means the ALTA Loan Policy (2006 form, as modified by the applicable North Carolina endorsements) issued by the Title Company in the amount of the Loan Amount, insuring the Deed of Trust as a valid first-priority lien on the Land and Improvements subject only to the Permitted Exceptions, together with all endorsements required by Section 4.1(h).\\n\\n(yyy) \\\"**Total Project Costs**\\\" means, as of any date of determination, the aggregate of all Project Costs, determined in accordance with the Approved Budget as the same may be revised with the Lender's consent pursuant to Section 6.3, and including, for the avoidance of doubt, the Existing Mortgage Payoff Amount and all pre-closing costs properly capitalised as Project Costs [*see Drafting Note 1(c)*].\\n\\n(zzz) \\\"**UCC**\\\" means the Uniform Commercial Code as in effect in the State of North Carolina.\\n:::\\n\\n## 1.2 Additional Defined Terms.\\n\\nThe following terms have the meanings given to them in the Sections indicated: \\\"**Bankruptcy Action**\\\" (Section 12.4); \\\"**Compliance Certificate**\\\" (Section 11.3); \\\"**Debt Service Coverage Ratio**\\\" or \\\"**DSCR**\\\" (Section 11.1(b)); \\\"**Extension Fee**\\\" (Section 21.2(e)); \\\"**Extension Option**\\\" (Section 21.1); \\\"**Interest Rate Cap**\\\" (Section 21.2(f)); \\\"**Late Charge**\\\" (Section 3.9); \\\"**Loan-to-Cost Ratio**\\\" or \\\"**LTC**\\\" (Section 11.1(c)); \\\"**Loan-to-Value Ratio**\\\" or \\\"**LTV**\\\" (Section 11.1(d)); \\\"**Release Conditions**\\\" (Section 6.7); \\\"**Reporting Requirements**\\\" (Schedule 7); \\\"**SPE**\\\" (Section 12.1); \\\"**Stated Amount**\\\" (Section 7.1); \\\"**Working Capital Reserve**\\\" (Section 11.1(f)).\\n\\n## 1.3 Interpretation.\\n\\n::: {custom-style=\\\"SubPara\\\"}\\n(a) The words \\\"include\\\", \\\"includes\\\" and \\\"including\\\" are deemed to be followed by \\\"without limitation\\\". \\\"Hereof\\\", \\\"herein\\\", \\\"hereunder\\\" and similar words refer to this Agreement as a whole. The singular includes the plural and vice versa. References to \\\"$\\\" or \\\"dollars\\\" are to United States dollars. References to Articles, Sections, Schedules and Exhibits are to this Agreement. Headings are for convenience only and do not affect interpretation.\\n\\n(b) References to any statute or regulation include any amendment, replacement, re-enactment or successor provision and any rules and regulations promulgated thereunder. References to \\\"days\\\" mean calendar days unless Business Days are specified. If any period expires on a day that is not a Business Day, the period is extended to the next Business Day. If any payment is due on a day that is not a Business Day, the payment is due on the next Business Day, and interest accrues in the interim.\\n\\n(c) Where any provision of this Agreement conflicts with any provision of any other Loan Document, this Agreement controls as between the Lender and the Borrower, except that the terms of the Intercreditor Agreement control as between the Lender and the Mezzanine Lender, and the terms of the Deed of Trust control as to matters of record affecting the Land.\\n\\n(d) Each reference to a dollar amount that is stated in brackets, or that is accompanied by a reference to a Drafting Note, reflects an unresolved conflict or an open business point in the source documents and is not to be treated as agreed.\\n\\n(e) This Agreement is the product of negotiation between sophisticated parties represented by counsel and is not to be construed against any party as drafter.\\n\\n# ARTICLE 2 — THE LOAN; COMMITMENT; PURPOSE\\n\\n## 2.1 The Commitment; Single Commitment, Multiple Advances.\\n\\nSubject to the terms and conditions of this Agreement, the Lender agrees to make Advances to the Borrower from time to time during the Construction Period in an aggregate principal amount not to exceed the Commitment. The Loan is a single committed facility with multiple Advances, and is not a revolving facility. No amount repaid or prepaid may be reborrowed. Any portion of the Commitment that has not been advanced on or before the last day for Advances under Section 2.4 is automatically cancelled.\\n\\n::: {custom-style=\\\"DraftNote\\\"}\\n**Drafting Note 1 (Memo Issues A-2 and E-1).** The Term Sheet (§3.1) describes the Loan as \\\"a single advance facility, with loan proceeds to be disbursed in accordance with the approved draw schedule\\\", which is internally contradictory: a draw-scheduled construction loan is a multiple-advance facility under a single commitment. Section 2.1 adopts the substance (one commitment, staged advances) and corrects the label. In addition, the Term Sheet and the Credit Memorandum both fail to reconcile the Commitment with the 80% LTC covenant (see Section 2.6 and Drafting Note 2).\\n:::\\n\\n## 2.2 Purpose.\\n\\nThe proceeds of the Loan shall be used solely to fund Project Costs in accordance with the Approved Budget and the Draw Schedule, and for no other purpose. No proceeds of the Loan shall be used (i) to fund any cost that is not an approved line item of the Approved Budget, (ii) to fund any cost overrun, (iii) to repay the Mezzanine Loan, (iv) to make any distribution to any member of the Borrower or any Affiliate, other than payment of the Developer Fee strictly in accordance with Section 6.5(c), or (v) for any purpose that would violate Regulation U or Regulation X of the Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System.\\n\\n## 2.3 Note; Interest and Principal.\\n\\nThe Loan shall be evidenced by the Note and shall bear interest and be payable as provided in Article 3. The Loan is interest-only during the Construction Period and the Mini-Perm Period; no scheduled principal amortisation is required, and the outstanding principal balance, together with all accrued and unpaid interest, fees and other amounts, is due and payable in full on the Maturity Date unless earlier accelerated.\\n\\n## 2.4 Advance Period.\\n\\nNo Advance shall be made after the earlier of (i) the Construction Maturity Date and (ii) the date on which the Commitment is fully advanced or cancelled; provided that the Final Advance (Retainage release) may be made after Substantial Completion in accordance with Section 5.9, and any Advance in respect of an approved Change Order may be made during the Mini-Perm Period if, and only if, the Lender has approved such Change Order and sufficient undisbursed Commitment remains available.\\n\\n## 2.5 Conversion to Mini-Perm Period.\\n\\nIf Substantial Completion occurs on or before the Construction Maturity Date, the Loan shall convert to the Mini-Perm Period as of the first day of the calendar month following the month in which Substantial Completion occurs, and the rate of interest shall change accordingly on that date. If Substantial Completion has not occurred on or before the Construction Maturity Date, (i) the Loan shall nonetheless convert to the Mini-Perm Period and the rate of interest applicable to the Mini-Perm Period shall apply from the day following the Construction Maturity Date, (ii) the failure to achieve Substantial Completion by the Construction Maturity Date shall constitute an Event of Default under Section 16.1(f) unless waived in writing by the Lender, and (iii) the Lender's obligation to make further Advances shall terminate except as expressly provided in Section 5.9.\\n\\n## 2.6 Loan-to-Cost and Loan-to-Value Compliance at Closing; Reduction of the Commitment.\\n\\n::: {custom-style=\\\"SubPara\\\"}\\n(a) **LTC Condition.** It is a condition to the Lender's obligation to close that the Loan-to-Cost Ratio, determined as of the Closing Date on the basis of Total Project Costs and the Commitment (after giving effect to any reduction under this Section 2.6), shall not exceed **eighty percent (80%)**.\\n\\n(b) **LTV Condition.** It is a condition to the Lender's obligation to close that (i) the Loan-to-Value Ratio determined by dividing the Commitment by the As-Completed Value shall not exceed **sixty-five percent (65%)**, and (ii) the Loan-to-Value Ratio determined by dividing the Commitment by the As-Stabilized Value shall not exceed **sixty-five percent (65%)**.\\n\\n(c) **Mandatory Reduction or Cure.** If either the LTC Condition or the LTV Condition is not satisfied on the Closing Date, the Commitment shall be permanently reduced, without penalty or fee, to the largest amount that satisfies each such condition, being (i) in the case of the LTC Condition, the product of Total Project Costs multiplied by 80%, and (ii) in the case of the LTV Condition, the product of the As-Completed Value multiplied by 65%; and the Approved Budget, the Draw Schedule and each Guaranty denominated as a percentage of the Loan Amount shall be conformed accordingly. As an alternative to such reduction, the Borrower may satisfy the applicable condition by funding additional equity in an amount sufficient to cause Total Project Costs (in the case of the LTC Condition, after giving effect to the inclusion of the Existing Mortgage Payoff Amount and all pre-closing costs properly treated as Project Costs) to bear the required ratio to the Commitment. The Borrower shall deliver to the Lender, not later than five (5) Business Days before the Closing Date, a Compliance Certificate setting out the computations required by this Section 2.6.\\n\\n(d) **Conformed Amounts.** The parties acknowledge that, on the figures contained in the source documents, (i) LTC calculated as $47,500,000 ÷ $56,700,000 equals **83.77%**, which exceeds the 80% maximum, and the maximum Commitment at 80% LTC would be **$45,360,000**; and (ii) LTV calculated as $47,500,000 ÷ $72,800,000 equals **65.25%**, which exceeds the 65% maximum, and the maximum Commitment at 65% LTV would be **$47,320,000**. The binding constraint on those figures is the LTC Condition, and the conforming Commitment would be **$45,360,000**. The Loan Amount stated on the cover page and in Section 1.1(xx) is therefore subject to reduction in accordance with this Section 2.6.\\n:::\\n\\n::: {custom-style=\\\"DraftNote\\\"}\\n**Drafting Note 2 (Memo Issues A-1 and A-2).** This Section 2.6 is the operative mechanism for the two covenant breaches identified in the record. (a) **LTC.** The Term Sheet (§6.1) and the Credit Memorandum (§5.3, §9.1) both report LTC of 83.77% against an 80% maximum and a $2,140,000 \\\"shortfall\\\". The Credit Memorandum's proposed cure — a $2,140,000 cash equity escrow \\\"applied to project costs first\\\" — does **not** cure the breach, because LTC is senior debt divided by Total Project Costs, and depositing equity changes neither the numerator nor a denominator that is fixed by the Approved Budget (Total Project Costs remain $56,700,000 and the Commitment remains $47,500,000, producing the same 83.77%). An escrow cures LTC only if the Commitment is reduced dollar-for-dollar, or if additional costs are added to the denominator. Adding the $3,400,000 Existing Mortgage Payoff Amount (which is presently unfunded — see Drafting Note 5) would raise Total Project Costs to $60,100,000 and produce an LTC of 79.03% **if** the payoff is funded with equity rather than Loan proceeds. (b) **LTV.** The executed Term Sheet (§4 and §6.2) caps LTV at 65% on both an as-completed and as-stabilised basis. The Credit Memorandum (§6.1) applies a 70% policy maximum and reports the 65.25% as-completed LTV as a \\\"Pass\\\", which is incorrect as measured against the executed Term Sheet. The overage is $180,000. Both points require a business decision before the Loan Amount can be fixed. (c) **Schedule correction.** See Drafting Note 12 as to the Construction Maturity Date.\\n:::\\nMD\\nwc -w p1.md\"}"}], "input_tokens": 140050, "output_tokens": 8422, "finish_reason": "completed"}
{"turn": 13, "role": "tool", "result": "5233 p1.md\n", "tool_call_id": "call_00_i2f1kZnDO9TP3bNBueTA7759", "tool_name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && cat > p1.md <<'MD'\\n::: {custom-style=\\\"Title\\\"}\\nCONSTRUCTION-TO-MINI-PERMANENT LOAN AGREEMENT\\n:::\\n\\n::: {custom-style=\\\"Subtitle\\\"}\\nTHE PIEDMONT AT BRIGHTLEAF — 601 AND 615 FOSTER STREET, DURHAM, NORTH CAROLINA\\n:::\\n\\n::: {custom-style=\\\"Subtitle\\\"}\\nby and between HARBORVIEW CAPITAL PARTNERS LLC, as Borrower, and PINNACLE SAVINGS BANK, N.A., as Lender\\n:::\\n\\n|  |  |\\n|:---|:---|\\n| **Lender:** | Pinnacle Savings Bank, N.A., a national banking association |\\n| **Lender's Loan No.:** | CRE-2025-0342 |\\n| **Borrower:** | Harborview Capital Partners LLC, a North Carolina limited liability company |\\n| **Loan Amount:** | $[47,500,000] (see Section 2.6 as to reduction of the Commitment) |\\n| **Guarantors:** | Elena Vasquez-Torres and Reginald K. Osei |\\n| **Property:** | 601 and 615 Foster Street, Durham, Durham County, North Carolina 27701 (Durham County Parcel IDs 0821-04-72-3341 and 0821-04-72-4102) |\\n| **Target Closing Date:** | February 28, 2025 |\\n| **Draft Date:** | Prepared by Ashford, Cromdale Consulting & Laine LLP, counsel to the Lender |\\n| **Status:** | **WORKING DRAFT — FOR DISCUSSION ONLY — NOT AN OFFER; SUBJECT TO CREDIT APPROVAL, DILIGENCE AND DOCUMENTATION** |\\n\\n::: {custom-style=\\\"DraftNote\\\"}\\n**PRELIMINARY NOTE TO THIS DRAFT.** This draft has been prepared from, and is intended to give effect to, (i) the Term Sheet dated January 10, 2025 executed by the Lender and the Borrower, (ii) the Senior Loan Committee Credit Memorandum dated January 22, 2025 for Loan No. CRE-2025-0342 (the \\\"Credit Memorandum\\\"), (iii) the appraisal of Ridgeline Appraisal Services Inc. dated November 15, 2024 (File RAS-2024-1147), (iv) the Preliminary Title Commitment of Aldersgate Title & Escrow Inc. No. NC-2024-88712 effective December 5, 2024, 