{"turn": 19, "role": "tool", "result": "26:**PRELIMINARY NOTE TO THIS DRAFT.** This draft has been prepared from, and is intended to give effect to, (i) the Term Sheet dated January 10, 2025 executed by the Lender and the Borrower, (ii) the Senior Loan Committee Credit Memorandum dated January 22, 2025 for Loan No. CRE-2025-0342 (the \"Credit Memorandum\"), (iii) the appraisal of Ridgeline Appraisal Services Inc. dated November 15, 2024 (File RAS-2024-1147), (iv) the Preliminary Title Commitment of Aldersgate Title & Escrow Inc. No. NC-2024-88712 effective December 5, 2024, (v) the Phase I Environmental Site Assessment of Sentinel Environmental Consulting LLC dated October 28, 2024 (Project SEC-2024-1147) and the Phase II investigation it summarises, (vi) the Borrower's organizational chart and operating agreement excerpts dated January 2025, and (vii) the Borrower's construction budget and draw schedule dated January 8, 2025. The source documents do not agree in all respects. Where the record is internally inconsistent or silent, this draft adopts a position, states it in brackets, and flags the point in a \"Drafting Note\" cross-referenced to the issue numbering used in our accompanying cover memorandum of even date. **All bracketed amounts, dates and alternative formulations remain subject to business-term agreement and to the Lender's credit approval; no bracketed item is to be treated as finally negotiated.** Nothing in the source documents constitutes a binding commitment by the Lender except Sections 22 and 23 of the Term Sheet.\n97:(q) \"**Construction Maturity Date**\" means [**August 28, 2027**] [*Alternative, if the parties accept the schedule correction described in Drafting Note 2: **December 31, 2027***], being the last day of the Construction Period.\n122:(cc) \"**Equity Deposit**\" means the funds required to be deposited by the Borrower in the Equity Deposit Account pursuant to Section 7.6, in the amount of **$[2,140,000]** [*see Drafting Note 1(d) and Section 2.6 as to the amount, the source and the application of such funds*].\n150:(qq) \"**Interest Reserve**\" means the interest reserve in the original amount of **$[4,850,000]** established and maintained in accordance with Article 7 [*see Drafting Note 3 as to the adequacy of such amount*].\n219:(yyy) \"**Total Project Costs**\" means, as of any date of determination, the aggregate of all Project Costs, determined in accordance with the Approved Budget as the same may be revised with the Lender's consent pursuant to Section 6.3, and including, for the avoidance of doubt, the Existing Mortgage Payoff Amount and all pre-closing costs properly capitalised as Project Costs [*see Drafting Note 1(c)*].\n237:(d) Each reference to a dollar amount that is stated in brackets, or that is accompanied by a reference to a Drafting Note, reflects an unresolved conflict or an open business point in the source documents and is not to be treated as agreed.\n248:**Drafting Note 1 (Memo Issues A-2 and E-1).** The Term Sheet (§3.1) describes the Loan as \"a single advance facility, with loan proceeds to be disbursed in accordance with the approved draw schedule\", which is internally contradictory: a draw-scheduled construction loan is a multiple-advance facility under a single commitment. Section 2.1 adopts the substance (one commitment, staged advances) and corrects the label. In addition, the Term Sheet and the Credit Memorandum both fail to reconcile the Commitment with the 80% LTC covenant (see Section 2.6 and Drafting Note 2).\n280:**Drafting Note 2 (Memo Issues A-1 and A-2).** This Section 2.6 is the operative mechanism for the two covenant breaches identified in the record. (a) **LTC.** The Term Sheet (§6.1) and the Credit Memorandum (§5.3, §9.1) both report LTC of 83.77% against an 80% maximum and a $2,140,000 \"shortfall\". The Credit Memorandum's proposed cure — a $2,140,000 cash equity escrow \"applied to project costs first\" — does **not** cure the breach, because LTC is senior debt divided by Total Project Costs, and depositing equity changes neither the numerator nor a denominator that is fixed by the Approved Budget (Total Project Costs remain $56,700,000 and the Commitment remains $47,500,000, producing the same 83.77%). An escrow cures LTC only if the Commitment is reduced dollar-for-dollar, or if additional costs are added to the denominator. Adding the $3,400,000 Existing Mortgage Payoff Amount (which is presently unfunded — see Drafting Note 5) would raise Total Project Costs to $60,100,000 and produce an LTC of 79.03% **if** the payoff is funded with equity rather than Loan proceeds. (b) **LTV.** The executed Term Sheet (§4 and §6.2) caps LTV at 65% on both an as-completed and as-stabilised basis. The Credit Memorandum (§6.1) applies a 70% policy maximum and reports the 65.25% as-completed LTV as a \"Pass\", which is incorrect as measured against the executed Term Sheet. The overage is $180,000. Both points require a business decision before the Loan Amount can be fixed. (c) **Schedule correction.** See Drafting Note 12 as to the Construction Maturity Date.\n---\n28:**Drafting Note 3 (Memo Issue F-4).** The Default Rate is the applicable contract rate plus 5.00%, which at a SOFR of approximately 4.35% (the rate used in the Credit Memorandum) produces a rate of approximately 12.60% to 12.85% per annum. North Carolina generally permits commercial borrowers to agree to any rate of interest (N.C.G.S. §24-2), but the enforceability of a post-default increase and of compounding has not been uniformly addressed, and the Default Rate should not be used as a penalty. Section 3.11 (Usury Savings) is included for that reason and the Lender's counsel should confirm the treatment before the Default Rate is applied.\n48:**Drafting Note 4 (Memo Issue F-1).** The Origination Fee, the Interest Reserve and the Lender's own transaction costs are all funded from Loan proceeds in Draw 1 (Term Sheet §9.2; Borrower's Detailed Budget lines 3.04, 3.06, 3.07 and 4.02). Financing closing costs from the Loan increases the effective LTC and reduces the Borrower's equity at risk, and is inconsistent with the Term Sheet's statement (§21.5) that the Borrower pays all such costs. The lender's counsel should confirm whether funding its own fees from Loan proceeds is permitted by the Lender's policy; the alternative is to require those amounts to be paid by the Borrower at Closing from the Equity Deposit.\n68:**Drafting Note 5.** The Term Sheet (§15) provides a five (5) day grace period for monetary defaults but does not provide for a Late Charge. The Late Charge in Section 3.9 is an addition to the agreed business terms and requires the Borrower's agreement.\n96:(d) **Appraisal.** The Lender's receipt and satisfactory review of the Appraisal, confirmation that the As-Completed Value is not less than **$72,800,000** and the As-Stabilized Value is not less than **$76,200,000**, and delivery of any addendum or recertification the Lender may require, including an addendum addressing the matters described in Drafting Note 6.\n98:(e) **Environmental.** (i) The Lender's receipt and satisfactory review of the Phase I ESA and the full Phase II ESA, each accompanied by a reliance letter in favour of the Lender; (ii) a copy of the NFA Letter and evidence of its current status; (iii) evidence that the **deed notice required by Condition 4 of the NFA Letter has been recorded** in the Durham County Registry (or, if not recorded, a written acknowledgement from NCDEQ that the NFA determination remains in effect and an irrevocable undertaking by the Borrower to record it within the period specified in Section 13.2); (iv) evidence that the **soil management plan required by Condition 3 of the NFA Letter has been approved by NCDEQ**; (v) evidence that the soil vapor mitigation system required by Condition 1 of the NFA Letter has been designed by a professional engineer licensed in North Carolina and is incorporated into the Approved Plans and the Construction Contract; and (vi) either (A) a written modification of the NFA Letter permitting residential use of the Restricted Area, (B) written confirmation from NCDEQ that residential occupancy of enclosed space above the Restricted Area is permitted subject to the installation and operation of the vapor mitigation system, or (C) a redesign of the Project, approved by the Lender, that eliminates residential occupancy above the Restricted Area, together with revised financial projections satisfactory to the Lender [*see Drafting Note 7 and Section 13.4*].\n104:(h) **Existing Mortgage.** Evidence of the satisfaction and discharge of the Existing Mortgage, comprising either (i) a recorded cancellation or certificate of satisfaction executed in accordance with N.C.G.S. §45-37, or (ii) the Existing Mortgage Payoff Amount held in escrow with the Title Company for disbursement at Closing and a payoff letter dated within thirty (30) days before the Closing Date, in each case sufficient to delete Special Exception 10 from Schedule B-II of the Title Commitment [*see Drafting Note 8*].\n106:(i) **Survey.** Delivery of the Survey, free of encroachments, overlaps, boundary-line disputes and gaps, confirming (i) the acreage of each parcel, (ii) that the two parcels are contiguous, (iii) the location of Foster Street relative to each parcel, (iv) the location, width and recordation of any access easement or public right-of-way relied upon for secondary access, and (v) the location of the area identified in the Phase II ESA as the Restricted Area, tied to metes and bounds [*see Drafting Note 9*].\n110:(k) **Architectural Review.** Evidence that the Brightleaf Historic District Association Architectural Review Committee has approved the Approved Plans, or that the sixty (60) day deemed-approval period under Section 4.3(d) of the Declaration recorded in Book 6984, Page 1155 (as amended) has expired without written action, or a written waiver [*see Drafting Note 10*].\n114:(m) **Contractor's Consents and Waivers.** Delivery of (i) a certificate of the Contractor that no labour has been performed and no materials have been furnished to the Land under the Construction Contract before the recording of the Deed of Trust, (ii) unconditional waivers of lien in statutory form under N.C.G.S. Chapter 44A from each contractor, subcontractor and materialman that performed the demolition, site clearing, grading, utility stubbing or environmental remediation work on the Land before Closing, together with evidence of payment in full therefor, and (iii) an owner's affidavit of no liens and a gap indemnity in favour of the Title Company [*see Drafting Note 11*].\n134:(w) **Flood Determination.** Delivery of a current standard flood hazard determination confirming that no portion of the Land or Improvements is located in a Special Flood Hazard Area, or, if any portion is, evidence of flood insurance in the amount required by applicable law and the Lender's policy [*see Drafting Note 13*].\n148:**Drafting Note 6 (Memo Issue A-8).** The Appraisal is dated November 15, 2024 but states that the appraiser reviewed the Preliminary Title Commitment \"dated December 5, 2024\" — a date some three weeks after the date of value and of the report. The Appraisal also states that the land use restriction \"is memorialised in a Declaration of Land Use Restrictions recorded at the Durham County Register of Deeds\", whereas the Phase I ESA (October 28, 2024) states that the deed notice had not been recorded and that the NCDEQ deadline for recording was November 29, 2024, and the Title Commitment (December 5, 2024) does not disclose any such declaration. The Lender should obtain an addendum to the Appraisal (a) correcting the dating inconsistency, (b) confirming the value conclusions if the 14 residential units above the Restricted Area cannot be delivered, and (c) identifying the recorded land use restriction instrument and its recording information. See also Drafting Note 7.\n178:(k) **Environmental Compliance.** For any work within the Restricted Area, the Borrower shall have delivered (i) the NCDEQ-approved soil management plan, (ii) evidence that the vapour mitigation system is being installed in accordance with the NFA Letter and the Approved Plans, and (iii) the certifications described in Section 13.5 [*see Drafting Note 7*].\n225:The Initial Advance shall be made on the Closing Date in the amount of **$[9,475,000]**, comprising approved soft costs of $[4,150,000], the Interest Reserve of $[4,850,000] and the Origination Fee of $[475,000], allocated as shown on Schedule 4. The portions of the Initial Advance representing the Interest Reserve and the Origination Fee shall be applied by the Lender directly to the Interest Reserve Account and to the Origination Fee, respectively. The portion representing soft costs shall be deposited in a soft cost escrow account maintained by the Title Company or the Lender and disbursed only as the underlying soft costs are actually incurred and evidenced to the Lender's satisfaction [*see Drafting Note 14*].\n238:(a) **Substantial Completion Deadline.** The Borrower shall cause Substantial Completion to occur on or before **the Construction Maturity Date** [*see Drafting Note 12 as to the inconsistency between this date and the projected substantial completion date of August 31, 2027*].\n249:The Final Advance, in an amount equal to the aggregate Retainage then held (which, if the Construction Contract is performed in full at the guaranteed maximum price, is **$[3,475,000]**), shall be made only upon satisfaction of the Release Conditions described in Section 6.7. The parties acknowledge that the Draw Schedule as delivered states the Retainage release amount as **$[3,275,000]**, which is $[200,000] less than ten percent (10%) of the guaranteed maximum price; the Draw Schedule is to be conformed to the Approved Budget and to this Section 5.9 [*see Drafting Note 15*].\n", "tool_call_id": "call_00_6bcHw8RqX8rkmUUf8E4v6563", "tool_name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && grep -n \\\"Drafting Note\\\" p1.md | head -20; echo ---; grep -n \\\"Drafting Note\\\" p2.md\"}"}
