ary 10, 2025 executed by\n      the Lender and the Borrower, (ii) the Senior Loan Committee Credit Memorandum\n      dated January 22, 2025 for Loan No. CRE-2025-0342 (the “Credit Memorandum”),\n      (iii) the appraisal of Ridgeline Appraisal Services Inc. dated November 15, 2024\n      (File RAS-2024-1147), (iv) the Preliminary Title Commitment of Aldersgate Title &\n      Escrow Inc. No. NC-2024-88712 effective December 5, 2024, (v) the Phase I\n      Environmental Site Assessment of Sentinel Environmental Consulting LLC dated\n      October 28, 2024 (Project SEC-2024-1147) and the Phase II investigation it\n      summarises, (vi) the Borrower’s organizational chart and operating agreement\n      excerpts dated January 2025, and (vii) the Borrower’s construction budget and\n      draw schedule dated January 8, 2025. The source documents do not agree in all\n      respects. Where the record is internally inconsistent or silent, this draft adopts a\n      position, states it in brackets, and flags the point in a “Drafting Note” cross-\n      referenced to the issue numbering used in our accompanying cover memorandum\n      of even date. All bracketed amounts, dates and alternative formulations\n      remain subject to business-term agreement and to the Lender’s credit\n      approval; no bracketed item is to be treated as finally negotiated. Nothing\n      in the source documents constitutes a binding commitment by the Lender except\n      Sections 22 and 23 of the Term Sheet.\n\n\n\n\n               Loan Agreement — The Piedmont at Brightleaf — Loan No. CRE-2025-0342\n\f                          DRAFT 2/--/2025 — PRIVILEGED & CONFIDENTIAL — ATTORNEY WORK PRODUCT\n\n\n\n\n                             TABLE OF ARTICLES\nArticle                                             Heading\n1                                                   Definitions and Interpretation\n2                                                   The Loan; Commitment; Purpose\n3                                                   Interest, Fees, Yield Protection and Payments\n4                                                   Conditions Precedent to Closing\n5                                                   Conditions Precedent to Each Advance; Draw\n                                                    Mechanics\n6                                                   Disbursement; Approved Budget; Change\n                                                    Orders; Retainage\n7                                                   Interest Reserve Account; Equity Deposit\n                                                    Account\n8                                                   Representations and Warranties\n9                                                   Affirmative Covenants\n", "tool_call_id": "call_00_sBzrrFvCJE6tDpOtY2AS9766", "tool_name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && pdftotext -layout -f 1 -l 3 thumbs/loan-agreement-draft.pdf - | head -70\"}"}
