{"turn": 60, "role": "tool", "result": "     A-1 | The as-completed LTV exceeds the 65% covenant at closing\n     Record. Term Sheet §4 states that “the Lender’s maximum loan-to-value\n     ratio shall not exceed 65% on an as-completed basis”, and §6.2 sets a 65%\n     maximum on both an as-completed and an as-stabilised basis. Term Sheet §4\n     and Credit Memorandum §6.1 both compute the as-completed LTV as\n     $47,500,000 ÷ $72,800,000 = 65.25%. Credit Memorandum §6.1 applies a\n     “Bank Policy” column of “Max 70%” and reports the metric as “Pass”; §12\n     repeats “maximum LTV (70% for construction loans)”.\n\n     Analysis. Measured against the executed Term Sheet, 65.25% exceeds\n     65.00% by 0.25 percentage points, or $180,000 (72,800,000 × 0.65 =\n     47,320,000). The Credit Memorandum never states this. There is no\n     evidence that the Senior Loan Committee was asked to approve a departure\n     from the agreed 65% covenant; the table presents the metric as compliant\n     because the comparator column was changed to the 70% policy ceiling. Two\n     distinct limits are being conflated: a policy maximum (70%) and a negotiated\n     term (65%). A covenant that is breached the moment it is made is\n     unenforceable in practice and creates an immediate default if the Lender\n     later wishes to rely on it.\n\n     Open. Whether the Senior Loan Committee approved 65% or 70% for this\n     transaction, and why the Term Sheet (the executed document) records 65%.\n\n     Recommendation. Either (a) reduce the Commitment to $47,320,000,\n     which satisfies the 65% covenant but is not the binding constraint (see A-2),\n     or (b) amend the covenant to 66% (or to 70% if that is genuinely the credit\n     approval) and record that decision in the Committee minutes and in any\n     amendment to the Term Sheet. Do not leave the documentation stating 65%\n     while underwriting to 70%. Draft §2.6(b) and (c) apply the 65% covenant and\n     provide for automatic reduction of the Commitment; Drafting Note 2 records\n     the conflict.\n\n     A-2 | LTC exceeds 80% and the proposed equity escrow does not cure\n", "tool_call_id": "call_00_fPdRZXnYKsjQlpUAdHcM2376", "tool_name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && pdftotext -layout thumbs/cover-memorandum.pdf - | sed -n '/A-1 | The as-completed/,/A-2 |/p' | head -45\"}"}
